window.SOURATE_DATA = {"numSourate":15,"nomSourate":"Al-Hijr","nomFr":"Al-Hijr","nomEn":"The Rocky Tract","nomArabe":"الحجر","lieu":"La Mecque","lieuEn":"Makkah","typeSourateLabel":"Sourate Mecquoise","typeSourateLabelEn":"Meccan Surah","typeSourateClasse":"mecquoise","ordreRev":54,"nbVersets":99,"versets":[{"numVerset":1,"texteArabe":"بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيمِ الر  تِلْكَ آيَاتُ الْكِتَابِ وَقُرْآنٍ مُبِينٍ","tradPropre":"Alif, Lâm, Râ. Voici les versets du Livre et d'une Lecture explicite.","tradEn":"Alif, Lām, Rā. These are the verses of the Book and a clear Qur’ān [i.e., recitation].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Alif, Lâm, Râ: Ces lettres isolées placées en ouverture de la sourate appartiennent au secret d'Allāh et démontrent le miracle inimitable du Coran, composé des mêmes lettres arabes que celles utilisées par les hommes. Ces versets éminents prouvent qu’ils ont été révélés par Allah. Ce sont des versets qui exposent en détail le monothéisme et les lois de la religion.","explicationEn":"1. This sūrah begins with the disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceeded in Sūrah Baqarah. These verses are very significant, which indicates that they are revealed from Allah. They are verses of a Qur’ān that clarifies monotheism and sacred laws.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015001","lienPrecedent":"sourate-14-verset-52.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-2.html"},{"numVerset":2,"texteArabe":"رُبَمَا يَوَدُّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لَوْ كَانُوا مُسْلِمِينَ","tradPropre":"[Le Jour du Jugement Dernier] les mécréants voudraient avoir été Musulmans [soumis].","tradEn":"Perhaps those who disbelieve will wish that they had been Muslims.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le Jour de la Résurrection, les mécréants souhaiteront avoir été musulmans lorsqu’ils comprendront la vanité de leur mécréance dans le bas monde.","explicationEn":"2. On the Day of Judgement, when things become clear to them, the disbelievers will wish they were Muslim. The falsity of their ways in the world will be made clear to them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015002","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-1.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-3.html"},{"numVerset":3,"texteArabe":"ذَرْهُمْ يَأْكُلُوا وَيَتَمَتَّعُوا وَيُلْهِهِمُ الْأَمَلُ  فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُونَ","tradPropre":"Laisse-les manger, jouir (un temps), et être distraits par l'espoir; car bientôt ils sauront!","tradEn":"Let them eat and enjoy themselves and be diverted by [false] hope, for they are going to know.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, laisse ces dénégateurs manger comme des bestiaux, jouir des plaisirs passagers du bas monde et être distrait par l’espoir de la foi et des bonnes œuvres. Ils sauront qu’ils sont perdants lorsqu’ils comparaîtront face à Allah le Jour de la Résurrection","explicationEn":"3. O Messenger, leave these beliers to eat as the beasts eat, and to avail themselves of the finite pleasures of the world and let their hopes distract them from faith and righteous actions. They will come to know the loss they are in when they face Allah on the Day of Judgement.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015003","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-2.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-4.html"},{"numVerset":4,"texteArabe":"وَمَا أَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَرْيَةٍ إِلَّا وَلَهَا كِتَابٌ مَعْلُومٌ","tradPropre":"Or Nous ne détruisons aucune cité sans qu'elle n'ait eu [un terme fixé en] une Ecriture connue.","tradEn":"And We did not destroy any city but that for it was a known decree.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous ne décidons d’anéantir une cité habitée par des dénégateurs injustes que lorsque sort est déterminé au préalable dans la connaissance d’Allah. Une fois décidé, cet anéantissement ne peut être ni avancé ni reporté.","explicationEn":"4. For each oppressive town that became destroyed, Allah already knew of its fixed time. The destruction will neither come before or after its time.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015004","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-3.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-5.html"},{"numVerset":5,"texteArabe":"مَا تَسْبِقُ مِنْ أُمَّةٍ أَجَلَهَا وَمَا يَسْتَأْخِرُونَ","tradPropre":"Nulle communauté ne devance son terme, ni ne le retarde.","tradEn":"No nation will precede its term, nor will they remain thereafter.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Aucune communauté n’est anéantie avant que son terme n’arrive à échéance et son anéantissement ne peut être reporté lorsque son terme échoit. Par conséquent, que les injustes ne se fassent pas d’illusions sur le répit qu’Allah leur accorde.","explicationEn":"5. A nation will not be destroyed before its appointed time, and its destruction will not be delayed when its time arrives. The wrongdoers should not have hope in Allah delaying their fate.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015005","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-4.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-6.html"},{"numVerset":6,"texteArabe":"وَقَالُوا يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِي نُزِّلَ عَلَيْهِ الذِّكْرُ إِنَّكَ لَمَجْنُونٌ","tradPropre":"Et ils (les mecquois) disent: «O toi sur qui on a fait descendre le Coran, tu es certainement fou!","tradEn":"And they say, \"O you upon whom the message has been sent down, indeed you are mad.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les mécréants de la Mecque dirent au Messager: Ô celui qui prétend que le Rappel lui a été révélé, cette revendication fait de toi un aliéné se comportant avec folie.","explicationEn":"6. The disbelievers from Makkah said to the Messenger (peace be upon him): O you to whom the remembrance was revealed (as the Messenger himself used to claim), your claims make you out to be one who is possessed, and you behave as possessed people do.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015006","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-5.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-7.html"},{"numVerset":7,"texteArabe":"لَوْ مَا تَأْتِينَا بِالْمَلَائِكَةِ إِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصَّادِقِينَ","tradPropre":"Pourquoi ne nous es-tu pas venu avec les Anges, si tu es du nombre des véridiques?»","tradEn":"Why do you not bring us the angels, if you should be among the truthful?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Pourquoi ne t’es-tu pas fait accompagner par des anges, afin qu’ils attestent que ce que tu dis est vrai et pourquoi n’as-tu pas demandé que nous soyons anéantis pour notre mécréance?","explicationEn":"7. Why do you not call forth the angels to testify on your behalf, or why do you not ask for us to be destroyed because of our disbelief?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015007","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-6.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-8.html"},{"numVerset":8,"texteArabe":"مَا نُنَزِّلُ الْمَلَائِكَةَ إِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ وَمَا كَانُوا إِذًا مُنْظَرِينَ","tradPropre":"Nous ne faisons descendre les Anges qu'avec la vérité; et alors, il ne leur sera pas accordé de répit [à ces impies].","tradEn":"We do not send down the angels except with truth; and they [i.e., the disbelievers] would not then be reprieved.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah répondit alors à leur requête de voir les anges: Nous ne faisons descendre les anges que lorsque la sagesse l’impose, c’est-à-dire lorsque votre anéantissement est imminent. De plus, dès lors où Nous faisons descendre des anges et qu’ils refusent de croire, aucun répit supplémentaire ne leur est accordé. Ils sont alors promptement punis.","explicationEn":"8. In response to their idea of having the angels brought forth, Allah said: I will not send the angels except when it becomes wise to do so, that is, when your time comes to be penalised. And if the angels were sent and they did not believe, then their punishment would become imminent.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015008","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-7.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-9.html"},{"numVerset":9,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا نَحْنُ نَزَّلْنَا الذِّكْرَ وَإِنَّا لَهُ لَحَافِظُونَ","tradPropre":"En vérité c'est Nous qui avons fait descendre le Coran, et c'est Nous qui en sommes gardien.","tradEn":"Indeed, it is We who sent down the message [i.e., the Qur’ān], and indeed, We will be its guardian.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Contrairement à la Bible qui, selon tous les spécialistes, a été transformée au cours des siècles, le Coran reste un texte rigoureusement intact, inchangé depuis plus de quatorze siècles, conformément à cette promesse du Seigneur de le préserver de toute altération.","explicationUnanime":"C’est Nous qui avons révélé le Coran au cœur du Prophète Muħammad en guise de rappel adressé aux gens et Nous le préserverons certainement des ajouts, des suppressions, des modifications et des altérations.","explicationEn":"9. I alone revealed this Qur’ān to the heart of Muhammad (peace be upon him) as a reminder for people. I will guard the Qur’ān from anything being added to it or subtracted from it, or anything in it being exchanged or altered.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015009","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-8.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-10.html"},{"numVerset":10,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِكَ فِي شِيَعِ الْأَوَّلِينَ","tradPropre":"Et nous avons certes envoyé, avant toi, [des Messagers] parmi les peuples des Anciens.","tradEn":"And We had certainly sent [messengers] before you, [O Muḥammad], among the sects of the former peoples.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, Nous avons envoyé avant toi des messagers aux peuples mécréants du passés et ceux-ci les ont démentis. Le fait que ton peuple ne croit pas en toi n’est donc pas exceptionnel.","explicationEn":"10. O Messenger, I sent before you messengers to prior groups of disbelievers and they belied them. So you are not an exceptional messenger from the perspective of being made out as a liar by your people.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015010","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-9.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-11.html"},{"numVerset":11,"texteArabe":"وَمَا يَأْتِيهِمْ مِنْ رَسُولٍ إِلَّا كَانُوا بِهِ يَسْتَهْزِئُونَ","tradPropre":"Et pas un Messager ne leur est venu sans qu'ils s'en soient moqués.","tradEn":"And no messenger would come to them except that they ridiculed him.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Aucun messager n’a été envoyé aux peuples mécréants du passé sans qu’il n’ait été démenti et raillé.","explicationEn":"11. Previous groups of disbelievers did not receive a messenger except that they belied and ridiculed him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015011","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-10.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-12.html"},{"numVerset":12,"texteArabe":"كَذَالِكَ نَسْلُكُهُ فِي قُلُوبِ الْمُجْرِمِينَ","tradPropre":"C'est ainsi que Nous faisons pénétrer (la mécréance) dans les cœurs des coupables.","tradEn":"Thus do We insert it [i.e., denial] into the hearts of the criminals.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tout comme Nous avons suscité la dénégation dans les cœurs de ces peuples, Nous la suscitons dans les cœurs des polythéistes de la Mecque pour leur refus de croire et leur entêtement.","explicationEn":"12. As I left the lies in the hearts of those nations, I will leave it as well in the hearts of the Makkahn idolaters, because of their opposition and stubbornness.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015012","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-11.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-13.html"},{"numVerset":13,"texteArabe":"لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِهِ  وَقَدْ خَلَتْ سُنَّةُ الْأَوَّلِينَ","tradPropre":"Ils ne croiront pas en lui [le Messager ou le Coran] bien que se soit accompli le sort traditionnel des anciens.","tradEn":"They will not believe in it, while there has already occurred the precedent of the former peoples.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils ne croient pas au Coran révélé à Muħammad mais l’habitude qu’a Allah d’anéantir les dénégateurs est bien établie. Que ces dénégateurs qui te démentent en tirent un enseignement.","explicationEn":"13. They do not believe in this Qur’ān that was revealed to Muhammad (peace be upon him). Allah’s custom in destroying those who bely their messengers has occurred before, so the beliers should take that into consideration.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015013","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-12.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-14.html"},{"numVerset":14,"texteArabe":"وَلَوْ فَتَحْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ بَابًا مِنَ السَّمَاءِ فَظَلُّوا فِيهِ يَعْرُجُونَ","tradPropre":"Et même si Nous ouvrions pour eux une porte du ciel, et qu'ils pussent y monter,","tradEn":"And [even] if We opened to them a gate from the heaven and they continued therein to ascend,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces dénégateurs s’obstinent à te démentir même après que la vérité leur soit parvenue accompagnée de preuves manifestes et ils continueront à te démentir même si on leur ouvrait une porte du Ciel vers laquelle il ne cesserait de monter.","explicationEn":"14. These liars will remain stubborn even if the truth became obvious to them through clear proofs, even if I opened for them a door from the heavens and they continued to ascend through it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015014","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-13.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-15.html"},{"numVerset":15,"texteArabe":"لَقَالُوا إِنَّمَا سُكِّرَتْ أَبْصَارُنَا بَلْ نَحْنُ قَوْمٌ مَسْحُورُونَ","tradPropre":"ils diraient: «Vraiment nos yeux sont voilés. Mais plutôt, nous sommes des gens ensorcelés».","tradEn":"They would say, \"Our eyes have only been dazzled. Rather, we are a people affected by magic.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Malgré cela, ils ne t’accorderaient pas de crédit et diraient: Nos yeux sont couverts et incapables de voir. Ce que nous voyons n’est que l’effet d’un ensorcellement dont nous sommes victimes.","explicationEn":"15. They would not believe, and they said: Our eyes could no longer see, and what we saw was the effects of magic, so we are bewitched.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015015","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-14.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-16.html"},{"numVerset":16,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ جَعَلْنَا فِي السَّمَاءِ بُرُوجًا وَزَيَّنَّاهَا لِلنَّاظِرِينَ","tradPropre":"Certes Nous avons placé dans le ciel des constellations et Nous l'avons embelli pour ceux qui regardent.","tradEn":"And We have placed within the heaven great stars and have beautified it for the observers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons placé dans le Ciel des étoiles très brillantes grâce auxquelles s’orientent les gens qui voyagent dans l’obscurité de la terre ferme et de la mer et Nous les avons embellies à l’attention de ceux qui les regardent afin qu’ils en déduisent l’immensité du pouvoir d’Allah.","explicationEn":"16. We placed in the heavens great stars so as to guide people on their travels in the darkness of the desert and the sea. We also created them for those who ponder them, so that they would come to understand the ability of Allah, may He be glorified.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015016","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-15.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-17.html"},{"numVerset":17,"texteArabe":"وَحَفِظْنَاهَا مِنْ كُلِّ شَيْطَانٍ رَجِيمٍ","tradPropre":"Et Nous l'avons protégé contre tout diable banni.","tradEn":"And We have protected it from every devil expelled [from the mercy of Allāh]","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons préservé le Ciel de tout démon exclu de la miséricorde d’Allah.","explicationEn":"17. We protected the heavens from every satan that is rejected from Allah’s mercy.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015017","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-16.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-18.html"},{"numVerset":18,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا مَنِ اسْتَرَقَ السَّمْعَ فَأَتْبَعَهُ شِهَابٌ مُبِينٌ","tradPropre":"A moins que l'un d'eux parvienne subrepticement à écouter, une flamme brillante alors le poursuit.","tradEn":"Except one who steals a hearing and is pursued by a clear burning flame.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Si l’un d’eux parvient à s’approcher suffisamment près des habitants du monde céleste au point de pourvoir les écouter, un corps céleste incandescent le poursuit alors et le consume.","explicationEn":"18. Except for those who try to secretly listen to the high realm, they will be struck with a flaming meteor and they will be burned.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015018","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-17.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-19.html"},{"numVerset":19,"texteArabe":"وَالْأَرْضَ مَدَدْنَاهَا وَأَلْقَيْنَا فِيهَا رَوَاسِيَ وَأَنْبَتْنَا فِيهَا مِنْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ مَوْزُونٍ","tradPropre":"Et quant à la terre, Nous l'avons étalée et y avons placé des montagnes (immobiles) et y avons fait pousser toute chose harmonieusement proportionnée.","tradEn":"And the earth - We have spread it and cast therein firmly set mountains and caused to grow therein [something] of every well-balanced thing.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Qui en assurent la stabilité.","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons étendu la Terre afin que les gens s’y établissent et Nous l’avons stabilisée par des montagnes immobiles qui l’empêchent de vaciller. Nous y avons aussi fait pousser des variétés de plantes déterminées selon ce que requiert la sagesse.","explicationEn":"19. I flattened the earth so that people would dwell on it, and we placed sturdy mountains on it so that it (i.e. the earth) would not shake the people, and I planted in it a variety of crops [...]","precisionConsensus":"Tafsīr d'At-Tabarī & d'Al-Qurtubī : Commentant « Wa al-arda madadnāhā », l'imam At-Tabarī et l'imam Al-Qurtubī rapportent d'après Ibn ‘Abbās et Qatādah qu'Allāh a étalé et aplani la Terre (Basatnāhā) sur la face des eaux à partir de La Mecque (Umm Al-Qurā), puis y a jeté de lourdes montagnes pour l'empêcher de pencher ou de trembler.","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015019","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-18.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-20.html"},{"numVerset":20,"texteArabe":"وَجَعَلْنَا لَكُمْ فِيهَا مَعَايِشَ وَمَنْ لَسْتُمْ لَهُ بِرَازِقِينَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous y avons placé des vivres pour vous, et (placé aussi pour vous) des êtres que vous ne nourrissez pas.","tradEn":"And We have made for you therein means of living and [for] those for whom you are not providers.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Comme les bestiaux et les montures.","explicationUnanime":"Ô gens, Nous avons placé sur Terre des nourritures et des boissons qui vous permettent de survivre dans ce bas monde. Nous y avons aussi placé des nourritures et des boissons pour d’autres créatures, humaines et animales, dont vous n’êtes pas capables d’assurer la subsistance.","explicationEn":"20. O people, I have placed for you on the earth foods and drinks that would sustain you so long as you are in the worldly life.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015020","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-19.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-21.html"},{"numVerset":21,"texteArabe":"وَإِنْ مِنْ شَيْءٍ إِلَّا عِنْدَنَا خَزَائِنُهُ وَمَا نُنَزِّلُهُ إِلَّا بِقَدَرٍ مَعْلُومٍ","tradPropre":"Et il n'est rien dont Nous n'ayons les réserves et Nous ne le faisons descendre que dans une mesure déterminée.","tradEn":"And there is not a thing but that with Us are its depositories, and We do not send it down except according to a known [i.e., specified] measure.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il n’existe pas de chose utile aux gens et aux bêtes que Nous ne soyons pas capables de faire exister et de mettre au service des gens. Nous n’en faisons exister qu’une quantité déterminée dans la mesure de ce que dictent Notre sagesse et Notre volonté.","explicationEn":"21. For all that benefits people and animals I am able to produce it and benefit people with it. I do not provide such things except according to a specific quantity determined by My wisdom and will.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015021","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-20.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-22.html"},{"numVerset":22,"texteArabe":"وَأَرْسَلْنَا الرِّيَاحَ لَوَاقِحَ فَأَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَاءِ مَاءً فَأَسْقَيْنَاكُمُوهُ وَمَا أَنْتُمْ لَهُ بِخَازِنِينَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous envoyons les vents fécondants; et Nous faisons alors descendre du ciel une eau dont Nous vous abreuvons et que vous n'êtes pas en mesure de conserver.","tradEn":"And We have sent the fertilizing winds and sent down water from the sky and given you drink from it. And you are not its retainers.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Les vents qui, par leur action sur les nuages, donnent naissance à la pluie et qui participent à la fécondation des arbres en transportant le pollen.<br><br><strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> C’est Nous qui la conservons sous forme notamment de sources, de puits et de rivières, afin qu’elle reste à la disposition des hommes tout au long de l’année.","explicationUnanime":"Nous envoyons les vents féconder les nuages puis Nous faisons descendre de ces nuages fécondés de la pluie dont Nous vous abreuvons. Ô gens, vous n’avez pas le pouvoir de faire des réserves de cette eau en la transformant en sources et en puits. Allah seul en est capable.","explicationEn":"22. I sent the winds to fertilise the cloud, and I sent rain down from the fertilised clouds and I nourished you from rain water. O people, you are not containers of this water on earth in springs and wells, rather Allah is the One Who contains the water in them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015022","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-21.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-23.html"},{"numVerset":23,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّا لَنَحْنُ نُحْيِي وَنُمِيتُ وَنَحْنُ الْوَارِثُونَ","tradPropre":"Et c'est bien Nous qui donnons la vie et donnons la mort, et c'est Nous qui sommes l'héritier [de tout].","tradEn":"And indeed, it is We who give life and cause death, and We are the Inheritor.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est Nous qui faisons revivre les morts: une première fois en les créant à partir de rien puis une seconde fois en les ressuscitant après leur mort et Nous faisons aussi mourir les vivants lorsqu’ils épuisent leur durée de vie. Nous seuls resterons afin d’hériter de la Terre et de ce qu’elle contient.","explicationEn":"23. I revive the dead by creating them out of nothing and resurrecting them after death. And I cause the living to die when their time comes. I am the One Who will remain and inherit the earth and whatever is upon it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015023","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-22.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-24.html"},{"numVerset":24,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ عَلِمْنَا الْمُسْتَقْدِمِينَ مِنْكُمْ وَلَقَدْ عَلِمْنَا الْمُسْتَأْخِرِينَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous connaissons certes ceux qui parmi vous ont avancé et Nous connaissons ceux qui tardent encore.","tradEn":"And We have already known the preceding [generations] among you, and We have already known the later [ones to come].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous savons qui parmi vous naîtra ou mourra précocement et savons également qui naîtra ou mourra tardivement.","explicationEn":"24. I know of who was born and died before you, and of those who will be born and die after. Nothing of that is hidden from Me.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015024","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-23.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-25.html"},{"numVerset":25,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ يَحْشُرُهُمْ  إِنَّهُ حَكِيمٌ عَلِيمٌ","tradPropre":"Certes, c'est ton Seigneur qui les rassemblera. Car c'est Lui le Sage, l'Omniscient.","tradEn":"And indeed, your Lord will gather them; indeed, He is Wise and Knowing.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, ton Seigneur est Celui qui les rassemblera tous le Jour de la Résurrection afin de récompenser le bienfaisant pour sa bienfaisance et le malfaisant pour sa malfaisance. Il est Sage dans Sa gestion et rien n’échappe à Sa connaissance.","explicationEn":"25. O Messenger, your Lord will gather them all on the Day of Judgment in order to credit the good doer for his good deeds, and the evil doer for his sins. He is Wise in His arrangement and knowledgeable. Nothing is hidden from Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015025","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-24.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-26.html"},{"numVerset":26,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْإِنْسَانَ مِنْ صَلْصَالٍ مِنْ حَمَإٍ مَسْنُونٍ","tradPropre":"Nous créâmes l'homme d'une argile crissante, extraite d'une boue malléable.","tradEn":"And We did certainly create man out of clay from an altered black mud.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons créé Adam d’une argile sèche qui lorsqu’elle est tapotée produit un son, à partir d’une argile noire qui est devenue malodorante avec le temps pour être restée à la même place.","explicationEn":"26. I created Adam from dried clay, if it is struck it sounds. This clay that he was created from is black and of an altered scent beacuse of the duration it has been left.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015026","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-25.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-27.html"},{"numVerset":27,"texteArabe":"وَالْجَانَّ خَلَقْنَاهُ مِنْ قَبْلُ مِنْ نَارِ السَّمُومِ","tradPropre":"Et quant au djinn, Nous l'avions auparavant créé d'un feu d'une chaleur ardente.","tradEn":"And the jinn We created before from scorching fire.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons créé les djinns bien avant Adam d’un feu ardent.","explicationEn":"27. I created the father of the jinn from scolding fire before I created Adam (upon him be peace).","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015027","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-26.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-28.html"},{"numVerset":28,"texteArabe":"وَإِذْ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ إِنِّي خَالِقٌ بَشَرًا مِنْ صَلْصَالٍ مِنْ حَمَإٍ مَسْنُونٍ","tradPropre":"Et lorsque ton Seigneur dit aux Anges: «Je vais créer un homme d'argile crissante, extraite d'une boue malléable,","tradEn":"And [mention, O Muḥammad], when your Lord said to the angels, \"I will create a human being out of clay from an altered black mud.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, rappelle-toi lorsque ton Seigneur dit aux anges et à Iblîs qui était présent parmi eux: Je vais créer un être humain d’une argile sèche qui produit un son lorsqu’elle est tapotée, noire et malodorante.","explicationEn":"28. O Messenger, remember when Allah said to the angels and Iblis, who was with them: I will create a being from dried clay that rings when it is hit, it is black and of an altered scent.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015028","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-27.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-29.html"},{"numVerset":29,"texteArabe":"فَإِذَا سَوَّيْتُهُ وَنَفَخْتُ فِيهِ مِنْ رُوحِي فَقَعُوا لَهُ سَاجِدِينَ","tradPropre":"et dès que Je l'aurai harmonieusement formé et lui aurai insufflé Mon souffle de vie, jetez-vous alors, prosternés devant lui».","tradEn":"And when I have proportioned him and breathed into him of My [created] soul, then fall down to him in prostration.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ou : de Mon souffle de vie.","explicationUnanime":"Quand Je lui aurai donné une belle apparence et aurai achevé sa formation, prosternez-vous devant lui afin de Me prouver que vous M’obéissez et afin de le saluer.","explicationEn":"29. If I fashion his image and perfect his creation then prostrate to him in obedience to My command and to greet him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015029","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-28.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-30.html"},{"numVerset":30,"texteArabe":"فَسَجَدَ الْمَلَائِكَةُ كُلُّهُمْ أَجْمَعُونَ","tradPropre":"Alors, les Anges se prosternèrent tous ensemble,","tradEn":"So the angels prostrated - all of them entirely,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les anges obéirent tous et se prosternèrent conformément à ce que leur avait ordonné leur Seigneur.","explicationEn":"30. The angels obeyed, so they all prostrated as their Lord commanded them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015030","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-29.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-31.html"},{"numVerset":31,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا إِبْلِيسَ أَبَىٰ أَنْ يَكُونَ مَعَ السَّاجِدِينَ","tradPropre":"excepté Iblis qui refusa d'être avec les prosternés.","tradEn":"Except Iblees; he refused to be with those who prostrated.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"En revanche, Iblîs –qui était présent parmi les anges mais n’en est pas un– s’abstint de se prosterner devant Adam.","explicationEn":"31. As for Iblis, who was with the angels but was not one himself, refused to prostrate to Adam along with the angels.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015031","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-30.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-32.html"},{"numVerset":32,"texteArabe":"قَالَ يَا إِبْلِيسُ مَا لَكَ أَلَّا تَكُونَ مَعَ السَّاجِدِينَ","tradPropre":"Alors [Allah] dit: «O Iblis, pourquoi n'es-tu pas au nombre des prosternés?»","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"O Iblees, what is [the matter] with you that you are not with those who prostrate?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah dit à Iblîs après que celui-ci se soit abstenu de se prosterner devant Adam: Pour quelle raison t’es-tu abstenu de te prosterner avec les anges qui M’ont obéi?","explicationEn":"32. After Iblis refused to prostrate to Adam, Allah said to him: What kept you and prevented you from prostrating with the angels, who prostrated out of obedience to My command?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015032","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-31.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-33.html"},{"numVerset":33,"texteArabe":"قَالَ لَمْ أَكُنْ لِأَسْجُدَ لِبَشَرٍ خَلَقْتَهُ مِنْ صَلْصَالٍ مِنْ حَمَإٍ مَسْنُونٍ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «Je ne puis me prosterner devant un homme que Tu as créé d'argile crissante, extraite d'une boue malléable».","tradEn":"He said, \"Never would I prostrate to a human whom You created out of clay from an altered black mud.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Empli d’orgueil, Iblîs répondit: Il ne convient pas que je me prosterne devant un être humain que Tu as créé d’argile sèche qui auparavant était noire et malodorante.","explicationEn":"33. Iblis arrogantly said: It is not proper for me to prostrate to a being You created out of dried clay that used to be black, malleable clay.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015033","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-32.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-34.html"},{"numVerset":34,"texteArabe":"قَالَ فَاخْرُجْ مِنْهَا فَإِنَّكَ رَجِيمٌ","tradPropre":"- Et [Allah] dit: «Sors de là [du Paradis], car te voilà banni!","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"Then depart from it, for indeed, you are expelled.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah répliqua: Sors du Paradis car tu en es chassé.","explicationEn":"34. Allah said to Iblis: Exit from paradise, for you are banished.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015034","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-33.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-35.html"},{"numVerset":35,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ عَلَيْكَ اللَّعْنَةَ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ","tradPropre":"Et malédiction sur toi, jusqu'au Jour de la rétribution!»","tradEn":"And indeed, upon you is the curse until the Day of Recompense.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"La malédiction te poursuivra jusqu’au Jour de la Rétribution et tu seras exclus de Ma Miséricorde jusqu’à ce jour-là.","explicationEn":"35. Upon you is My damnation and banished you are from My mercy until the Day of Judgment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015035","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-34.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-36.html"},{"numVerset":36,"texteArabe":"قَالَ رَبِّ فَأَنْظِرْنِي إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ","tradPropre":"- Il dit: «O mon Seigneur, donne-moi donc un délai jusqu'au jour où ils (les gens) seront ressuscités».","tradEn":"He said, \"My Lord, then reprieve me until the Day they are resurrected.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Iblîs formula alors la requête suivante: Ô Seigneur, accorde-moi un répit et ne me fais pas mourir avant le Jour où les gens seront ressuscités.","explicationEn":"36. Iblis said: O Lord, allow me to live and do not cause me to die until the day that Adam and his offspring are resurrected.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015036","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-35.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-37.html"},{"numVerset":37,"texteArabe":"قَالَ فَإِنَّكَ مِنَ الْمُنْظَرِينَ","tradPropre":"[Allah] dit: «tu es de ceux à qui ce délai est accordé,","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"So indeed, you are of those reprieved","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tu es de ceux à qui J’ai accordé un répit et dont J’ai reporté la mort.","explicationEn":"37. Allah (the Exalted) said: You are of those who I will grant a long life.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015037","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-36.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-38.html"},{"numVerset":38,"texteArabe":"إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ الْوَقْتِ الْمَعْلُومِ","tradPropre":"jusqu'au jour de l'instant connu» [d'Allah].","tradEn":"Until the Day of the time well-known.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Je t’ai accordé un répit jusqu’au moment où toutes les créatures qui ne seront pas encore mortes devront mourir, c’est-à-dire lorsque le premier Souffle dans la Trompe sera effectué.","explicationEn":"38. Until the time when all created things will die, upon the first blow of the Horn.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015038","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-37.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-39.html"},{"numVerset":39,"texteArabe":"قَالَ رَبِّ بِمَا أَغْوَيْتَنِي لَأُزَيِّنَنَّ لَهُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلَأُغْوِيَنَّهُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ","tradPropre":"- Il dit: «O mon Seigneur, parce que Tu m'as induit en erreur, eh bien je leur enjoliverai la vie sur terre et les égarerai tous,","tradEn":"[Iblees] said, \"My Lord, because You have put me in error, I will surely make [disobedience] attractive to them [i.e., mankind] on earth, and I will mislead them all","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Iblîs dit: Ô Seigneur, puisque Tu m’a induis en erreur, j’embellirai aux êtres humains vivant sur la Terre les péchés et les égarerai tous du droit chemin.","explicationEn":"39. Iblis said: O Lord, because You misguided me, I will make sins on earth seem attractive to them, and I will lead them all astray from the straight path.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015039","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-38.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-40.html"},{"numVerset":40,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا عِبَادَكَ مِنْهُمُ الْمُخْلَصِينَ","tradPropre":"à l'exception, parmi eux, de Tes serviteurs élus.»","tradEn":"Except, among them, Your chosen servants.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Excepté ceux parmi Tes serviteurs que Tu as élus pour T’adorer.","explicationEn":"40. Except for those servants You select to be worshipful to You.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015040","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-39.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-41.html"},{"numVerset":41,"texteArabe":"قَالَ هَاذَا صِرَاطٌ عَلَيَّ مُسْتَقِيمٌ","tradPropre":"- «[Allah] dit: voici une voie droite [qui mène] vers Moi.","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"This is a path [of return] to Me [that is] straight.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah dit: Voici une voie médiane qui mène vers Moi.","explicationEn":"41. Allah said: This is a straight path that leads to Me.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015041","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-40.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-42.html"},{"numVerset":42,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ عِبَادِي لَيْسَ لَكَ عَلَيْهِمْ سُلْطَانٌ إِلَّا مَنِ اتَّبَعَكَ مِنَ الْغَاوِينَ","tradPropre":"Sur Mes serviteurs tu n'auras aucune autorité, excepté sur celui qui te suivra parmi les dévoyés.","tradEn":"Indeed, My servants - no authority will you have over them, except those who follow you of the deviators.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tu n’auras sur Mes serviteurs fidèles aucun pouvoir ni aucune emprise. Tu ne pourras donc tenter que les égarés qui te suivent.","explicationEn":"42. You have no power or sway over tempting My sincere servants, except for those who follow you who are led astray.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015042","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-41.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-43.html"},{"numVerset":43,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ لَمَوْعِدُهُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ","tradPropre":"Et l'Enfer sera sûrement leur lieu de rendez-vous à tous.","tradEn":"And indeed, Hell is the promised place for them all.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"L’Enfer est assurément promis à Iblîs et à tous les égarés qui le suivent.","explicationEn":"43. Hellfire is the promised abode of Iblis and all those who follow him who have been led astray.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015043","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-42.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-44.html"},{"numVerset":44,"texteArabe":"لَهَا سَبْعَةُ أَبْوَابٍ لِكُلِّ بَابٍ مِنْهُمْ جُزْءٌ مَقْسُومٌ","tradPropre":"Il a sept portes; et chaque porte en a sa part déterminée».","tradEn":"It has seven gates; for every gate is of them [i.e., Satan's followers] a portion designated.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Autre sens : celle-ci dispose de sept niveaux. Chacun accueillera un nombre déterminé de damnés.","explicationUnanime":"L’Enfer a sept portes par lesquelles ils entrent et par chaque porte entrera un nombre déterminé de disciples deIblîs.","explicationEn":"44. Hellfire has seven doors through which they enter. For each of its doors, there is a known amount of the followers of Iblis who will enter through it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015044","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-43.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-45.html"},{"numVerset":45,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ الْمُتَّقِينَ فِي جَنَّاتٍ وَعُيُونٍ","tradPropre":"Certes, les pieux seront dans des jardins avec des sources.","tradEn":"Indeed, the righteous will be within gardens and springs,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceux qui craignent leur Seigneur, en se conformant à Ses commandements et en délaissant Ses interdits seront dans des vergers irrigués par des sources.","explicationEn":"45. Those who were mindful of Allah, by obeying His command and staying away from disobedience will have gardens and springs.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015045","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-44.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-46.html"},{"numVerset":46,"texteArabe":"ادْخُلُوهَا بِسَلَامٍ آمِنِينَ","tradPropre":"«Entrez-y en paix et en sécurité».","tradEn":"[Having been told], \"Enter it in peace, safe [and secure].\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"On leur dira à leur entrée: Entrez, vous serez exempts de toute maladie et ne ressentirez aucune crainte.","explicationEn":"46. When they enter, it will be said to them: Enter it with safety from any misfortune and security from any fears.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015046","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-45.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-47.html"},{"numVerset":47,"texteArabe":"وَنَزَعْنَا مَا فِي صُدُورِهِمْ مِنْ غِلٍّ إِخْوَانًا عَلَىٰ سُرُرٍ مُتَقَابِلِينَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous aurons arraché toute rancune de leurs poitrines: et ils se sentiront frères, faisant face les uns aux autres sur des lits.","tradEn":"And We will remove whatever is in their breasts of resentment, [so they will be] brothers, on thrones facing each other.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous aurons fait disparaître de leurs cœurs toute rancune et toute hostilité. Ils seront alors tels des frères qui s’aiment, assis sur des banquettes les uns face aux autres.","explicationEn":"47. I removed what was in their chests of enmity and envy. They are brethren beloved to one another, sitting upon thrones and looked upon one another.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015047","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-46.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-48.html"},{"numVerset":48,"texteArabe":"لَا يَمَسُّهُمْ فِيهَا نَصَبٌ وَمَا هُمْ مِنْهَا بِمُخْرَجِينَ","tradPropre":"Nulle fatigue ne les y touchera. Et on ne les en fera pas sortir.","tradEn":"No fatigue will touch them therein, nor from it will they [ever] be removed.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils ne ressentiront au Paradis plus aucune fatigue et ils n’en seront pas chassés. Ils y demeureront plutôt éternellement.","explicationEn":"48. Fatigue does not affect them, and they will not be made to leave it. Rather, they will remain in it forever.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015048","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-47.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-49.html"},{"numVerset":49,"texteArabe":"۞ نَبِّئْ عِبَادِي أَنِّي أَنَا الْغَفُورُ الرَّحِيمُ","tradPropre":"Informe Mes serviteurs que c'est Moi le Pardonneur, le Très Miséricordieux.","tradEn":"[O Muḥammad], inform My servants that it is I who am the Forgiving, the Merciful,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, informe Mes serviteurs que Je pardonne à ceux parmi eux qui se repentent, et que Je suis miséricordieux avec eux.","explicationEn":"49. O Messenger, inform My servants that I am the Forgiving towards whomever of them repents, and I am Merciful to them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015049","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-48.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-50.html"},{"numVerset":50,"texteArabe":"وَأَنَّ عَذَابِي هُوَ الْعَذَابُ الْأَلِيمُ","tradPropre":"et que Mon châtiment est certes le châtiment douloureux.","tradEn":"And that it is My punishment which is the painful punishment.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Informe-les également que Mon châtiment est douloureux. Qu’ils se repentent donc à Moi afin d’obtenir Mon pardon et échappent à Mon châtiment.","explicationEn":"50. And inform them that My punishment is the severe punishment, so they should repent to Me so they can receive My forgiveness and be safe from My punishment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015050","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-49.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-51.html"},{"numVerset":51,"texteArabe":"وَنَبِّئْهُمْ عَنْ ضَيْفِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ","tradPropre":"Et informe-les au sujet des hôtes d'Abraham","tradEn":"And inform them about the guests of Abraham,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Informe-les aussi au sujet des hôtes d’Abraham: c’était des anges qui lui apportaient la bonne nouvelle de la naissance prochaine d’un fils ainsi que la nouvelle de l’anéantissement du peuple de Loth.","explicationEn":"51. And inform them of the story of the guests of Ibrahim (peace be with him) that were angels who came to give him glad tidings of a child, and news of the destructions of the people of Lot.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015051","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-50.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-52.html"},{"numVerset":52,"texteArabe":"إِذْ دَخَلُوا عَلَيْهِ فَقَالُوا سَلَامًا قَالَ إِنَّا مِنْكُمْ وَجِلُونَ","tradPropre":"Quand ils entrèrent chez lui et dirent: «Salâm» - Il dit: «Nous avons peur de vous».","tradEn":"When they entered upon him and said, \"Peace.\" [Abraham] said, \"Indeed, we are fearful [i.e., apprehensive] of you.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsqu’ils entrèrent chez lui, ils lui dirent «Salâmun (Paix)». Il leur répondit avec une salutation meilleure et leur présenta un veau rôti, pensant que c’était des êtres humains mais voyant qu’ils n’étaient pas intéressés par ce met, il leur dit: Vous nous faites peur.","explicationEn":"52. When they came to him and said, Peace. He answered them with a greeting that was better than theirs and presented them with a roasted calf for them to eat because he thought that they were human. When they did not eat of it he said: We are afraid of you.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015052","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-51.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-53.html"},{"numVerset":53,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا لَا تَوْجَلْ إِنَّا نُبَشِّرُكَ بِغُلَامٍ عَلِيمٍ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «N'aie pas peur! Nous t'annonçons une bonne nouvelle, [la naissance] d'un garçon plein de savoir».","tradEn":"[The angels] said, \"Fear not. Indeed, we give you good tidings of a learned boy.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les anges messagers lui dirent alors: Ne crains rien car nous allons t’annoncer ce qui va te réjouir: tu auras un garçon qui sera très savant.","explicationEn":"53. The Messenger from the Angels said: Do not be afraid! We will tell you something that will make you glad. You are going to have a son with great knowledge.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015053","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-52.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-54.html"},{"numVerset":54,"texteArabe":"قَالَ أَبَشَّرْتُمُونِي عَلَىٰ أَنْ مَسَّنِيَ الْكِبَرُ فَبِمَ تُبَشِّرُونَ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «M'annoncez-vous [cette nouvelle] alors que la vieillesse m'a touché? Que m'annoncez-vous donc?»","tradEn":"He said, \"Have you given me good tidings although old age has come upon me? Then of what [wonder] do you inform?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Etonné qu’on lui annonce qu’il aura un fils, Abraham leur demanda: M’annoncez-vous la nouvelle de la naissance d’un fils alors que j’ai atteint la vieillesse? Comment se fait-il donc que vous me fassiez cette annonce?","explicationEn":"54. Abraham, being surprised at the good news of a baby boy they gave him, said to them: Do you bring me this good news despite the fact that old age has reached me? What kind of good news are you bringing me?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015054","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-53.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-55.html"},{"numVerset":55,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا بَشَّرْنَاكَ بِالْحَقِّ فَلَا تَكُنْ مِنَ الْقَانِطِينَ","tradPropre":"- Ils dirent: «Nous t'annonçons la vérité. Ne sois donc pas de ceux qui désespèrent».","tradEn":"They said, \"We have given you good tidings in truth, so do not be of the despairing.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les messagers répondirent: Nous t’annonçons une vérité indubitable. Ne sois donc pas de ceux qui désespèrent de ce qu’on leur annonce.","explicationEn":"55. The Messengers from the Angels said to Abraham: We bring you good news of the truth in which there is no doubt, so do not be among those who despair from the good news we bring you.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015055","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-54.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-56.html"},{"numVerset":56,"texteArabe":"قَالَ وَمَنْ يَقْنَطُ مِنْ رَحْمَةِ رَبِّهِ إِلَّا الضَّالُّونَ","tradPropre":"- Il dit: «Et qui désespère de la miséricorde de son Seigneur, sinon les égarés?»","tradEn":"He said, \"And who despairs of the mercy of his Lord except for those astray?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Abraham dit: Qui d’autre que les déviants du droit chemin d’Allah désespèrent de la miséricorde de leur Seigneur?","explicationEn":"56. Abraham said: Does anyone despair from the mercy of his Lord but those who have deviated from Allah’s straight path?!","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015056","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-55.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-57.html"},{"numVerset":57,"texteArabe":"قَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكُمْ أَيُّهَا الْمُرْسَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Et il [leur] dit: «Que voulez-vous, ô envoyés d'Allah?»","tradEn":"[Abraham] said, \"Then what is your business [here], O messengers?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis il poursuivit: Quelle est la raison pour laquelle vous êtes venus, ô vous qui êtes envoyés par Allah?","explicationEn":"57. Abraham said: What is the matter that has brought you - O Messengers - from Allah?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015057","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-56.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-58.html"},{"numVerset":58,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا إِنَّا أُرْسِلْنَا إِلَىٰ قَوْمٍ مُجْرِمِينَ","tradPropre":"- Ils dirent: «En vérité, nous sommes envoyés à des gens criminels,","tradEn":"They said, \"Indeed, we have been sent to a people of criminals,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les anges messagers répondirent: Allah nous a envoyés afin d’anéantir un peuple extrêmement corrupteur et maléfique: le peuple de Loth.","explicationEn":"58. The Messenger from the Angels said: Allah has sent us to destroy a people who are guilty of great corruption and evil, the people of Lot.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015058","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-57.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-59.html"},{"numVerset":59,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا آلَ لُوطٍ إِنَّا لَمُنَجُّوهُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ","tradPropre":"à l'exception de la famille de Lot que nous sauverons tous","tradEn":"Except the family of Lot; indeed, we will save them all","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous les anéantirons tous excepté la famille et les disciples croyants de Loth qui seront épargnés.","explicationEn":"59. Except the family of Lot and the believers that follow him for they will not be included in the destruction and We will save them all from it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015059","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-58.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-60.html"},{"numVerset":60,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا امْرَأَتَهُ قَدَّرْنَا  إِنَّهَا لَمِنَ الْغَابِرِينَ","tradPropre":"sauf sa femme.«Nous (Allah) avions déterminé qu'elle sera du nombre des exterminés.","tradEn":"Except his wife.\" We [i.e., Allāh] decreed that she is of those who remain behind.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons cependant jugé que son épouse restera et sera anéantie également.","explicationEn":"60. Except for his wife, for We have decreed her to be one of those who stay behind included in the destruction.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015060","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-59.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-61.html"},{"numVerset":61,"texteArabe":"فَلَمَّا جَاءَ آلَ لُوطٍ الْمُرْسَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Puis lorsque les envoyés vinrent auprès de la famille de Lot","tradEn":"And when the messengers came to the family of Lot,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Plus tard, lorsque les anges messagers se présentèrent à la famille de Loth sous une apparence humaine,","explicationEn":"61. When the Messengers from the Angels came to the family of Lot in the form of men.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015061","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-60.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-62.html"},{"numVerset":62,"texteArabe":"قَالَ إِنَّكُمْ قَوْمٌ مُنْكَرُونَ","tradPropre":"celui-ci dit: «Vous êtes [pour moi] des gens inconnus».","tradEn":"He said, \"Indeed, you are people unknown.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Loth leur dit: Vous m’êtes inconnus.","explicationEn":"62. Lot (peace be with him) said to them: I do not recognise you, nor do I know who you are.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015062","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-61.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-63.html"},{"numVerset":63,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا بَلْ جِئْنَاكَ بِمَا كَانُوا فِيهِ يَمْتَرُونَ","tradPropre":"- Ils dirent: «Nous sommes plutôt venus à toi en apportant (le châtiment) à propos duquel ils doutaient.","tradEn":"They said, \"But we have come to you with that about which they were disputing,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils répondirent: Ne crains rien. Nous sommes venus abattre sur les tiens un châtiment destructeur dont ils doutaient.","explicationEn":"63. The Messengers from the Angels said to Lot: Do not fear! We have brought to you - O Lot - the destructive punishment that your people have doubts about.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015063","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-62.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-64.html"},{"numVerset":64,"texteArabe":"وَأَتَيْنَاكَ بِالْحَقِّ وَإِنَّا لَصَادِقُونَ","tradPropre":"Et nous venons à toi avec la vérité. Et nous sommes véridiques.","tradEn":"And we have come to you with truth, and indeed, we are truthful.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous t’apportons aussi la vérité indubitable et nous sommes véridiques dans ce que nous t’annonçons.","explicationEn":"64. We have brought to you the truth in which there is no joke, and we are truthful in the information we give you.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015064","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-63.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-65.html"},{"numVerset":65,"texteArabe":"فَأَسْرِ بِأَهْلِكَ بِقِطْعٍ مِنَ اللَّيْلِ وَاتَّبِعْ أَدْبَارَهُمْ وَلَا يَلْتَفِتْ مِنْكُمْ أَحَدٌ وَامْضُوا حَيْثُ تُؤْمَرُونَ","tradPropre":"Pars donc avec ta famille en parie de nuit et suis leurs arrières; et que nul d'entre vous ne se retourne. Et allez là où on vous le commande».","tradEn":"So set out with your family during a portion of the night and follow behind them and let not anyone among you look back and continue on to where you are commanded.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Emmène tes proches lorsque la plus grande partie de la nuit se sera écoulée et suis-les. Que personne parmi vous ne se retourne afin de voir ce qu’il adviendra des mécréants et partez là où Allah vous a ordonné de partir.","explicationEn":"65. So travel with your family after a portion of the night has passed. Travel behind them and let none of you look back to see what happens to them. Proceed to where Allah has instructed you to go.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015065","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-64.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-66.html"},{"numVerset":66,"texteArabe":"وَقَضَيْنَا إِلَيْهِ ذَالِكَ الْأَمْرَ أَنَّ دَابِرَ هَاؤُلَاءِ مَقْطُوعٌ مُصْبِحِينَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous lui annonçâmes cet ordre: que ces gens-là, au matin, seront anéantis jusqu'au dernier.","tradEn":"And We conveyed to him [the decree] of that matter: that those [sinners] would be eliminated by early morning.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Par le biais de la Révélation, Nous avons annoncé à Loth ce que nous avons décrété: l’anéantissement jusqu’au dernier des gens à l’aube.","explicationEn":"66. We made known to Lot by means of revelation the matter that We had decreed, which was that those people will be annihilated by the last of them being destroyed when morning comes.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015066","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-65.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-67.html"},{"numVerset":67,"texteArabe":"وَجَاءَ أَهْلُ الْمَدِينَةِ يَسْتَبْشِرُونَ","tradPropre":"Et les habitants de la ville (Sodome) vinrent [à lui] dans la joie.","tradEn":"And the people of the city came rejoicing.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Informés de la présence chez Loth de jeunes invités, les habitants de Sodome arrivèrent, ivres d’allégresse, sans savoir qu’il s’agissait d’anges à l’apparence humaine.","explicationUnanime":"Les habitants de Sodome se précipitèrent chez Loth, réjouis par la nouvelle de l’arrivée de ses hôtes et aspirant à s’adonner à la turpitude avec eux.","explicationEn":"67. The people of Sodom came rejoicing at the guests of Lot, with the desire to commit indecency.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015067","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-66.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-68.html"},{"numVerset":68,"texteArabe":"قَالَ إِنَّ هَاؤُلَاءِ ضَيْفِي فَلَا تَفْضَحُونِ","tradPropre":"- Il dit: «Ceux-ci sont mes hôtes, ne me déshonorez donc pas.","tradEn":"[Lot] said, \"Indeed, these are my guests, so do not shame me.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Loth leur dit: Ces gens sont mes hôtes. Ne me déshonorez pas par ce que vous voulez commettre avec eux.","explicationEn":"68. Lot said to them: These people are my guests, so do not disgrace me by what you want with them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015068","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-67.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-69.html"},{"numVerset":69,"texteArabe":"وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَلَا تُخْزُونِ","tradPropre":"Et craignez Allah. Et ne me couvrez pas d'ignominie.»","tradEn":"And fear Allāh and do not disgrace me.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Craignez Allah en délaissant cette turpitude et ne me discréditez pas avec vos pratiques immondes.","explicationEn":"69. Fear Allah by leaving this indecent behaviour and do not humiliate me by this heinous act of yours.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015069","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-68.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-70.html"},{"numVerset":70,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا أَوَلَمْ نَنْهَكَ عَنِ الْعَالَمِينَ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Ne t'avions-nous pas interdit de [recevoir] du monde?»","tradEn":"They said, \"Have we not forbidden you from [protecting] people?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les siens lui rétorquèrent: Ne t’avons-nous pas défendu de recevoir des gens?","explicationEn":"70. His people said to him: Did we not forbid you from hosting anyone? One who provides a warning has in effect excused himself for taking someone to account for not abiding by it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015070","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-69.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-71.html"},{"numVerset":71,"texteArabe":"قَالَ هَاؤُلَاءِ بَنَاتِي إِنْ كُنْتُمْ فَاعِلِينَ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «Voici mes filles, si vous voulez faire [quelque chose]!»","tradEn":"[Lot] said, \"These are my daughters - if you would be doers [of lawful marriage].\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> C’est-à-dire, les femmes de mon peuple, selon nombre d’exégètes, que Loth semble les inviter ici à prendre pour épouses.","explicationUnanime":"Loth dit aux assaillants afin de se dédouaner auprès de ses hôtes: Voici mes filles parmi vos femmes. Epousez-les donc si ce que vous recherchez est la satisfaction de vos besoins charnels.","explicationEn":"71. Lot (peace be with him) said to them: These are the women of my people, who are like daughters to me. Marry them if you want to satisfy your desires.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015071","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-70.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-72.html"},{"numVerset":72,"texteArabe":"لَعَمْرُكَ إِنَّهُمْ لَفِي سَكْرَتِهِمْ يَعْمَهُونَ","tradPropre":"Par ta vie! ils se confondaient dans leur délire.","tradEn":"By your life, [O Muḥammad], indeed they were, in their intoxication, wandering blindly.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Par ta vie ô Messager, le peuple de Loth se débattait dans l’emprise que leur désir charnel avait sur eux.","explicationEn":"72. By your life - O Messenger - the people of Lot wander blindly in pursuit of their lusts.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015072","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-71.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-73.html"},{"numVerset":73,"texteArabe":"فَأَخَذَتْهُمُ الصَّيْحَةُ مُشْرِقِينَ","tradPropre":"Alors, au lever du soleil le Cri (la catastrophe) les saisit.","tradEn":"So the shriek seized them at sunrise.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est alors qu’un cri terrible et destructeur les surprit à l’aube.","explicationEn":"73. The destructive punishment seized them at the time of sunrise.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015073","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-72.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-74.html"},{"numVerset":74,"texteArabe":"فَجَعَلْنَا عَالِيَهَا سَافِلَهَا وَأَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ حِجَارَةً مِنْ سِجِّيلٍ","tradPropre":"Et Nous renversâmes [la ville] de fond en comble et fîmes pleuvoir sur eux des pierres d'argile dure.","tradEn":"And We made the highest part [of the city] its lowest and rained upon them stones of hard clay.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Suite à ce cri, Nous avons renversé la cité sens dessus dessous et Nous avons fait pleuvoir sur eux de l’argile durcie.","explicationEn":"74. We turned their towns upside down and rained on them a shower of petrified clay.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015074","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-73.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-75.html"},{"numVerset":75,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ فِي ذَالِكَ لَآيَاتٍ لِلْمُتَوَسِّمِينَ","tradPropre":"Voilà vraiment des preuves, pour ceux qui savent observer!","tradEn":"Indeed in that are signs for those who discern.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces scènes de l’anéantissement du peuple de Loth constituent des signes adressés à ceux qui sont capables de les méditer.","explicationEn":"75. In the incident mentioned about the punishment that descended on the people of Lot there are signs for those who ponder.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015075","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-74.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-76.html"},{"numVerset":76,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّهَا لَبِسَبِيلٍ مُقِيمٍ","tradPropre":"Elle [cette ville] se trouvait sur un chemin connu de tous.","tradEn":"And indeed, they [i.e., those cities] are [situated] on an established road.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Sachant que de surcroît, les cités du peuple de Loth sont situées dans une région fréquentée, que les voyageurs peuvent contempler.","explicationEn":"76. The towns of the people of Lot are on an existing road and can be seen by travellers who pass by.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015076","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-75.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-77.html"},{"numVerset":77,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ فِي ذَالِكَ لَآيَةً لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ","tradPropre":"Voilà vraiment une exhortation pour les croyants!","tradEn":"Indeed in that is a sign for the believers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"On trouve également dans ces scènes des leçons adressés aux croyants afin qu’ils les méditent.","explicationEn":"77. In that which occurred there is a sign for the believers to take lesson from.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015077","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-76.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-78.html"},{"numVerset":78,"texteArabe":"وَإِنْ كَانَ أَصْحَابُ الْأَيْكَةِ لَظَالِمِينَ","tradPropre":"Et les habitants d'al-Aïka étaient [aussi] des injustes.","tradEn":"And the companions of the thicket [i.e., the people of Madyan] were [also] wrongdoers,","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Nom du bosquet d’arbres touffus et entrelacés que vénérait ce peuple auquel fut envoyé le prophète Chou’ayb (Tafsîr ibn Kathîr).","explicationUnanime":"Le peuple de Chu’ayb, les habitants du village de l’arbre aux branches entremêlées, était un peuple injuste puisqu’ils mécroyaient en Allah et démentaient Chu’ayb, leur messager.","explicationEn":"78. The people of Shuayb, who lived in a town surrounded by intertwined trees, were wrongdoers; because of their denial of Allah and rejection of His Messenger, Shuayb (peace be with him).","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015078","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-77.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-79.html"},{"numVerset":79,"texteArabe":"فَانْتَقَمْنَا مِنْهُمْ وَإِنَّهُمَا لَبِإِمَامٍ مُبِينٍ","tradPropre":"Nous Nous sommes donc vengés d'eux. Et ces deux [cités], vraiment, sont sur une route bien évidente [que vous connaissez].","tradEn":"So We took retribution from them, and indeed, both [cities] are on a clear highway.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Celle du peuple de Loth et celle du peuple de Chou’ayb.","explicationUnanime":"Nous nous sommes donc vengés d’eux en les châtiant. Les cités du peuple de Loth et celles du peuple de Chu’ayb sont situées dans des lieux fréquentés et accessibles à ceux qui passent à proximité.","explicationEn":"79. We took retribution from them when the punishment seized them. The towns of the people of Lot and the dwellings of the people of Shuayb are on a path clear to those who pass by.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015079","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-78.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-80.html"},{"numVerset":80,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ كَذَّبَ أَصْحَابُ الْحِجْرِ الْمُرْسَلِينَ","tradPropre":"Certes, les gens d'al-Hijr ont traité de menteurs les messagers.","tradEn":"And certainly did the companions of al-Ḥijr [i.e., the Thamūd] deny the messengers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les Thamûd qui habitaient Al-Ħijr (Hegra), une cité située entre le Hejaz et la Syrie, ont démenti tous les messagers lorsqu’ils démentirent leur prophète Şâliħ.","explicationEn":"80. Indeed the Thamud, who were the people of Hijr (a place between Hijaz and the Levant) had in effect rejected all the Messengers when they rejected their prophet, Salih (peace be with him.)","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015080","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-79.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-81.html"},{"numVerset":81,"texteArabe":"وَآتَيْنَاهُمْ آيَاتِنَا فَكَانُوا عَنْهَا مُعْرِضِينَ","tradPropre":"Nous leur avons montré Nos miracles, mais ils s'en étaient détournés.","tradEn":"And We gave them Our signs, but from them they were turning away.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous leur avons fourni des arguments et des indices de la véracité de ce qu’il apportait de son Seigneur, dont le miracle de la chamelle, mais ils n’accordèrent aucune importance à ces indices.","explicationEn":"81. We gave them proofs and signs to indicate his truthfulness in what he brought from his Lord. One of these was the she-camel. But they did not take a lesson from those signs and paid no attention to them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015081","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-80.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-82.html"},{"numVerset":82,"texteArabe":"وَكَانُوا يَنْحِتُونَ مِنَ الْجِبَالِ بُيُوتًا آمِنِينَ","tradPropre":"Et ils taillaient des maisons dans les montagnes, vivant en sécurité.","tradEn":"And they used to carve from the mountains, houses, feeling secure.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils façonnaient le roc des montagnes pour y creuser des maisons où ils se tenaient à l’abri de ce qu’ils redoutaient.","explicationEn":"82. They used to carve out dwellings in the rocks of the mountains in which they lived safe from that which they feared.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015082","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-81.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-83.html"},{"numVerset":83,"texteArabe":"فَأَخَذَتْهُمُ الصَّيْحَةُ مُصْبِحِينَ","tradPropre":"Puis, au matin, le Cri les saisit.","tradEn":"But the shriek seized them at early morning,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est un matin à l’aube que la foudre du châtiment s’abattit sur eux.","explicationEn":"83. Then the bolt of the punishment seized them in the morning.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015083","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-82.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-84.html"},{"numVerset":84,"texteArabe":"فَمَا أَغْنَىٰ عَنْهُمْ مَا كَانُوا يَكْسِبُونَ","tradPropre":"Ce qu'ils avaient acquis ne leur a donc point profité.","tradEn":"So nothing availed them [from] what they used to earn.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ni leurs richesses ni leurs demeures imposantes n’ont repoussé la colère d’Allah.","explicationEn":"84. The wealth and the dwellings that they had gained did not ward off Allah’s punishment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015084","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-83.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-85.html"},{"numVerset":85,"texteArabe":"وَمَا خَلَقْنَا السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا إِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ  وَإِنَّ السَّاعَةَ لَآتِيَةٌ  فَاصْفَحِ الصَّفْحَ الْجَمِيلَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous n'avons créé les cieux et la terre, et ce qui est entre eux, que pour une juste raison. Et l'Heure [sans aucun doute] arrivera! Pardonne-[leur] donc d'un beau pardon.","tradEn":"And We have not created the heavens and earth and that between them except in truth. And indeed, the Hour is coming; so forgive with gracious forgiveness.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous n’avons pas créé les Cieux et la Terre et ce qu’il y a entre les deux vainement et sans raison profonde. Nous ne les avons en effet créés que pour une juste raison. Par ailleurs, l’Heure surviendra certainement. Détourne-toi donc, ô Messager, de ceux qui ne te croient pas et pardonne-leur d’une belle manière.","explicationEn":"85. We did not create the heavens and the earth and we did not create everything between them in vain without any wisdom. We only created all of that with a true purpose. The Hour will certainly come, so, O Messenger, ignore those who reject you and pardon them graciously.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015085","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-84.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-86.html"},{"numVerset":86,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ الْخَلَّاقُ الْعَلِيمُ","tradPropre":"Ton Seigneur, c'est Lui vraiment le grand Créateur, l'Omniscient.","tradEn":"Indeed, your Lord - He is the Knowing Creator.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, ton Seigneur est le Créateur de toute chose et Celui qui connaît le mieux ce qu’Il a créé.","explicationEn":"86. Your Lord, O Messenger, is the Creator and the Knower of everything.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015086","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-85.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-87.html"},{"numVerset":87,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَاكَ سَبْعًا مِنَ الْمَثَانِي وَالْقُرْآنَ الْعَظِيمَ","tradPropre":"Nous t'avons certes donné «les sept versets que l'on répète», ainsi que le Coran sublime.","tradEn":"And We have certainly given you, [O Muḥammad], seven of the often repeated [verses] and the great Qur’ān.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Les sept versets de la première sourate du Coran (Al-Fâtihah) que les fidèles répètent à plusieurs reprises en prière, selon la majorité des exégètes, ou les sept plus longues sourates du Coran, selon d’autres.","explicationUnanime":"Nous t’avons révélé sourate Al-Fâtiħah, la sourate aux sept versets redoublés, qui est aussi éminente que le Coran dans sa totalité.","explicationEn":"87. We have given you ‘The Opening (Sūrah Al-Fātiḥah)’ which consists of seven verses and We have given you the Grand Qur’ān.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015087","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-86.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-88.html"},{"numVerset":88,"texteArabe":"لَا تَمُدَّنَّ عَيْنَيْكَ إِلَىٰ مَا مَتَّعْنَا بِهِ أَزْوَاجًا مِنْهُمْ وَلَا تَحْزَنْ عَلَيْهِمْ وَاخْفِضْ جَنَاحَكَ لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ","tradPropre":"Ne regarde surtout pas avec envie les choses dont Nous avons donné jouissance temporaire à certains couples d'entre eux, ne t'afflige pas à leur sujet et abaisse ton aile pour les croyants.","tradEn":"Do not extend your eyes toward that by which We have given enjoyment to [certain] categories of them [i.e., the disbelievers], and do not grieve over them. And lower your wing [i.e., show kindness] to the believers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ne porte pas ton regard sur les jouissances variées mais passagères que Nous avons accordées aux mécréants, ne sois pas attristé par le démenti qu’ils t’opposent et sois accessible aux croyants.","explicationEn":"88. Do not extend your sight to the temporary enjoyments We have given to some classes of disbelievers and do not grieve over their rejection. Be humble with the believers.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015088","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-87.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-89.html"},{"numVerset":89,"texteArabe":"وَقُلْ إِنِّي أَنَا النَّذِيرُ الْمُبِينُ","tradPropre":"Et dis: «Je suis l'avertisseur évident» (d'un châtiment),","tradEn":"And say, \"Indeed, I am the clear warner\" -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, dis: Je suis l’avertisseur qui avertit avec éloquence du châtiment d’Allah.","explicationEn":"89. Say - O Messenger: I am indeed a warner of the punishment and I make clear that which will guide you.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015089","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-88.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-90.html"},{"numVerset":90,"texteArabe":"كَمَا أَنْزَلْنَا عَلَى الْمُقْتَسِمِينَ","tradPropre":"De même que Nous avons fait descendre [le châtiment] sur ceux qui ont juré (entre eux),","tradEn":"Just as We had revealed [scriptures] to the separators","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Selon certains commentateurs, ce verset, directement lié au verset 87 - les versets 88 et 89 n’étant qu’une incidente -, signifie en réalité : (Nous t’avons donné les sept versets sans cesse répétés et le sublime Coran) de même que Nous avons fait descendre Notre parole sur ceux qui ont divisé le Livre révélé.","explicationUnanime":"Je vous avertis d’un châtiment semblable à celui qui s’est abattu sur ceux qui ont divisé le Livre d’Allah en plusieurs parties, croyant en certaines et rejetant d’autres.","explicationEn":"90. I warn you of a punishment similar to that which Allah sent down on those who formed an alliance to deny the messengers.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015090","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-89.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-91.html"},{"numVerset":91,"texteArabe":"الَّذِينَ جَعَلُوا الْقُرْآنَ عِضِينَ","tradPropre":"ceux qui ont fait du Coran des fractions diverses, (pour créer des doutes).","tradEn":"Who have made the Qur’ān into portions.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils ont également divisé le Coran en parties qu’ils ont qualifiées de magie, de divination et de poésie.","explicationEn":"91. Those who accepts parts of the Qur’ān and allege other parts to be sorcery, soothsaying or poetry.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015091","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-90.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-92.html"},{"numVerset":92,"texteArabe":"فَوَرَبِّكَ لَنَسْأَلَنَّهُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ","tradPropre":"Par ton Seigneur! Nous les interrogerons tous","tradEn":"So by your Lord, We will surely question them all","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Par ton Seigneur, ô Messager, nous questionnerons le Jour de la Résurrection tous ceux qui ont divisé le Coran en plusieurs parties.","explicationEn":"92. By your Lord, O Messenger, I will on the Day of Judgement bring all those who break it into parts to account.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015092","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-91.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-93.html"},{"numVerset":93,"texteArabe":"عَمَّا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ","tradPropre":"sur ce qu'ils œuvraient.","tradEn":"About what they used to do.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous les interrogerons à propos de leur mécréance et de leurs actes de désobéissance commis dans ce bas monde.","explicationEn":"93. We will question them about the disbelief and sins they committed in the world.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015093","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-92.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-94.html"},{"numVerset":94,"texteArabe":"فَاصْدَعْ بِمَا تُؤْمَرُ وَأَعْرِضْ عَنِ الْمُشْرِكِينَ","tradPropre":"Expose donc clairement ce qu'on t'a commandé et détourne-toi des associateurs.","tradEn":"Then declare what you are commanded and turn away from the polytheists.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, proclame donc avec ostentation ce que ton Seigneur t’a ordonné de prêcher et n’accorde pas d’attention à ce que disent ou font les polythéistes.","explicationEn":"94. So announce, O Messenger, the invitation towards Allah that He has instructed you to do and do not pay any attention to what the idolaters say and do.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015094","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-93.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-95.html"},{"numVerset":95,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا كَفَيْنَاكَ الْمُسْتَهْزِئِينَ","tradPropre":"Nous t'avons effectivement défendu vis-à-vis des railleurs.","tradEn":"Indeed, We are sufficient for you against the mockers","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ne les crains pas non plus car Nous nous chargeons de te protéger de l’hostilité des chefs mécréants de Qoraych qui te raillent.","explicationEn":"95. Do not be afraid of them, for we are enough for you against those leaders of disbelief from the Quraysh who mock at you.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015095","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-94.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-96.html"},{"numVerset":96,"texteArabe":"الَّذِينَ يَجْعَلُونَ مَعَ اللَّهِ إِلَاهًا آخَرَ  فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُونَ","tradPropre":"Ceux qui associent à Allah une autre divinité. Mais ils sauront bientôt.","tradEn":"Who make [equal] with Allāh another deity. But they are going to know.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils ont adopté des divinités avec Allah et ils connaîtront la sinistre conséquence de leur polythéisme.","explicationEn":"96. Those who take another deity along with Allah. They will soon come to know the evil outcome of their associating partners with Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015096","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-95.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-97.html"},{"numVerset":97,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ نَعْلَمُ أَنَّكَ يَضِيقُ صَدْرُكَ بِمَا يَقُولُونَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous savons certes que ta poitrine se serre, à cause de ce qu'ils disent.","tradEn":"And We already know that your breast is constrained by what they say.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, Nous savons que tu es exaspéré par leur démenti et leurs railleries.","explicationEn":"97. We know that your heart, O Messenger, is constrained by the rejection and mockery of you that emanates from them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015097","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-96.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-98.html"},{"numVerset":98,"texteArabe":"فَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ وَكُنْ مِنَ السَّاجِدِينَ","tradPropre":"Glorifie donc Ton Seigneur par Sa louange et sois de ceux qui se prosternent;","tradEn":"So exalt [Allāh] with praise of your Lord and be of those who prostrate [to Him].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Refugie-toi donc auprès d’Allah en excluant de Lui ce qui ne Lui sied pas et en Le louant par la mention des attributs de Sa perfection. Sois également de ceux qui adorent Allah et Le prient. Tout cela te guérira de ton exaspération.","explicationEn":"98. So resort to Allah by declaring His transcendence from everything not appropriate for Him, and by praising Him with the attributes of His perfection; and be one of those who worship Allah and pray to Him. In that there is a cure for the strain on your heart.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015098","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-97.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-15-verset-99.html"},{"numVerset":99,"texteArabe":"وَاعْبُدْ رَبَّكَ حَتَّىٰ يَأْتِيَكَ الْيَقِينُ","tradPropre":"et adore ton Seigneur jusqu'à ce que te vienne la certitude (la mort).","tradEn":"And worship your Lord until there comes to you the certainty [i.e., death].","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> La mort, selon la majorité des commentateurs.","explicationUnanime":"En outre, adore continuellement ton Seigneur tant que tu es en vie jusqu’à ce que la mort te saisisse dans cet état.","explicationEn":"99. Go on worshipping your Lord and continue doing so as long as you live until death comes to you in that state.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"015099","lienPrecedent":"sourate-15-verset-98.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-16-verset-1.html"}]};